  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below normal temperatures continue this weekend\ninto early next week. \n\nAs low pressure moves into the Canadian Maritimes this weekend \nand high pressure builds to our west, northwesterly flow will \ncontinue to usher in cold air into the region. This will keep \ntemperatures slightly below normal through the weekend into \nearly next week. Early morning clouds have kept temperatures\nmuch warmer than expected, so canceled freeze warning and frost\nadvisory soon. Growing season ends per regional agreements on \nNovember 15th, so this will be the last frost/freeze headline of\nthe year. No further will be issued by our office until Spring \n2027.\n\nIn addition to the colder temperatures, winds will be gusty \nduring the day due to a tight pressure gradient across the area \nthrough the weekend with winds gusts of 20-30 mph possible.\n\nWith the cold air and northwest flow, there will also be the \npossibility for some lake effect/lake enhanced snow or rain \nshowers in the Poconos and higher elevations of Sussex County, \nNew Jersey as well. Brief periods of reduced visibility are \npossible, but little to no accumulation is expected. Conditions \nare not favorable for any snow squall development. Regardless, \nalways reduce speed and turn on low beam headlights anytime it \nsnows or visibility becomes reduced.\n\nTemps gradually moderate as we head toward the middle of next\nweek.",
